# Generated knowledge-graph output (rebuilt locally by the graphify tool)
graphify-out/
**/graphify-out/
andro-prime-vault/
.graphify_detect.json

# Local Claude state — but DO track project skills (shared infrastructure)
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
.agents/
.mcp.json

# Vendored skills installed by `npx skills add <owner>/<repo>`. The real files land
# in .agents/skills/ (ignored above) and are SYMLINKED into .claude/skills/. Committing
# the symlink stores a link whose target is not in the repo, so it resolves to nothing
# in any other checkout. Track our own skills, never the vendored ones.
# Add a line here for each new `skills add` install. `skills-lock.json` at the repo root
# IS tracked deliberately: it is the manifest that says which of these should exist.
.claude/skills/supabase/
.claude/skills/supabase-postgres-best-practices/

# Secrets / env files (never commit real secrets)
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# Backup and temp files
*.backup
*.tmp

# Build intermediates: build.js regenerates these from decks/ + covers.js.
andro-prime/06_marketing/content/instagram/carousel-prototype/slides/*/

# Published marketing media. Plan step 3.4, gate D3 ruled 2026-08-14: git holds the recipe, Drive
# holds what humans touch, Storage holds what a machine publishes from, and the database holds only
# the URI. `frontend/public/` is for genuine site chrome ONLY — the 110 carousel files committed on
# 2026-08-13 were content, and they are now in the Supabase `content` bucket, published and verified
# by publish-media.js. The manifest that records every published URL and hash IS committed.
#
# Untracking does not shrink history: the existing ~90 MB stays unless every commit hash is
# rewritten, which is not worth it at 113 MB total. This changes the trajectory, which is the part
# that compounds.
andro-prime/09_website-app/frontend/public/carousel/

# fanout harvest cache (paid SERP payloads, re-derivable; keep the staging CSV instead)
andro-prime/06_marketing/seo-ai-search/.fanout-harvest-*.json

# AI-actor film working media (Kit 2 "Same Programme", 2026-09-09). Same gate D3 rule as the
# carousel above: git holds the recipe, Drive holds the media. 208 MB of stage 1-4 stills and
# clips, most of it rejected takes kept for audit. The production log beside the storyboard IS committed and is the recipe:
# it carries every job_id, so any frame or clip can be re-fetched or re-generated from it.
#
# NOTE 2026-09-09: this was `kit2-same-programme/*/`, which excluded the DIRECTORIES. Git cannot
# re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so that pattern also swallowed the
# `.json` recipe sidecars sitting next to each asset — the recipe would have been lost with the
# media it exists to recover. An hour of A6 work (the S6b frames and their clips) had already
# gone unrecorded this way: bytes on disk, job_ids nowhere, recoverable only from the vendor's
# own history. Ignore the MEDIA by extension instead, so sidecars stay tracked.
andro-prime/06_marketing/content-machine/assets/kit2-same-programme/**/*.png
andro-prime/06_marketing/content-machine/assets/kit2-same-programme/**/*.jpg
andro-prime/06_marketing/content-machine/assets/kit2-same-programme/**/*.jpeg
andro-prime/06_marketing/content-machine/assets/kit2-same-programme/**/*.webp
andro-prime/06_marketing/content-machine/assets/kit2-same-programme/**/*.mp4
andro-prime/06_marketing/content-machine/assets/kit2-same-programme/**/*.mov

# Packaging renders. Heavy design artefacts, superseded often; the approved pack art is recorded
# in 02_brand/STATE.md with its date and job_id rather than committed as bytes.
# NOTE: `*` does not cross a `/`, so the single-level pattern below missed any SUBFOLDER of
# renders/ — the first one created (kit2-shotlist-2026-09-09, 94 MB) was fully stageable while
# STATE.md asserted these were ignored. The `**` line is what makes that assertion true.
andro-prime/02_brand/assets/packaging/renders/*.png
andro-prime/02_brand/assets/packaging/renders/**/*.png
